# Process for the next drain: .agents/skills/deficiency-cleanup/SKILL.md
#
# ── Format ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One dated block per entry. Every entry MUST carry a real `Decided-by:` line
# naming the human who authorised the descope and quoting their answer:
#
#   =========================================================================
#   ## From #<issue> — <title> (recorded <YYYY-MM-DD>)
#   <merge/PR ref + one-line state>
#
#   D1. <one-line deficiency>.
#       Decided-by: <human> on <YYYY-MM-DD> — asked "<the binary you put to
#                   them>", answered "<their verbatim answer>".
#       <what is less than maximal in the SHIPPED CODE>
#       Forward path: <the real work that would close it, and where it is
#                     tracked>.
#
# No `Decided-by:` line means it is not an entry. Do the work, or ask.
#
# Nothing in this repo reads this file. Recording here does not schedule the
# work, does not track it, and does not tell anyone — so every entry must also
# be surfaced on the issue and the PR, and stated plainly in the completion
# report. Three entries for one issue means the issue was not implemented:
# stop and say so.

