## From #1373 — logic glyph enrichment / GMN operator symbology plane (recorded 2026-08-10)
PR #1626, merged green. The issue's own deliverable — the modal SIGNS (□ ◇, their
codepoints, fixity/precedence and provenance) — ships and is gated. The entry below is
about a capability added BEYOND that deliverable.

D1. The modal-EVALUATION reasoner bridge never runs on shipped content: nothing in the
    pipeline calls it.
    Decided-by: Patrick Audley on 2026-08-10 — asked whether to wire the modal pass into
                reason_all_certified now, remove the bridge, or land and correct the
                record, answered "let's get this merged now, I really want to clean up
                these old branches and then attack all the CI fallout at once."
    crates/logic/src/foundation.rs evaluate_modal_formulas (:2441) has exactly ONE caller,
    foundation::evaluate (:3424). crates/pipeline never calls foundation::evaluate — the
    reasoner the bundle is built from is gmeow_logic::reason::reason_all_certified
    (crates/pipeline/src/stages/reason.rs:158), which carries no modal pass at all. The only
    production caller of foundation::evaluate is crates/conformance/src/run.rs:970, and
    crates/conformance is not a dependency of the shipped gmeow CLI. Observable consequence:
    generated/logic/inferred-closure.rdf12.ttl (149k lines) contains ZERO modal verdict
    instances — no logic:modalNecessityHolds / Fails / Undetermined, no
    logic:modalPossibilityHolds / Fails, no logic:modalCounterexampleWorld. Authoring a modal
    logic:Formula into any ingested source does NOT change this, because the evaluator is not
    on the path regardless of content. Secondary, and moot until the above is fixed: the
    evaluator decides a body that is a SINGLE GROUND ATOM only; a compound (∧/∨/¬/→) or
    nested-modal body is an explicit foundation_err hard fail, never a silent partial
    verdict, so no wrong modal verdict can be produced.
    Forward path: wire the modal pass into reason_all_certified so it runs on every bundle
                  build, then author a modal logic:Formula (body atom pinned by
                  logic:atomSubject/atomPredicate/atomObject, plus logic:modalEvalWorld and
                  one typed logic:overAccessibility) and a non-empty accessibility frame so
                  the verdict is real rather than a vacuous hold. Lifting the single-atom
                  body restriction (recursive per-world sub-formula evaluation) follows.
